From 70419191cca4fb09eb990866a580b66f6dd19467 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aadi Srivastava <aadisrivastava.iitm@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:54:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/24] Drop the back-edge poll of GC-free loops that provably
 terminate

The interior and carried pointers of the previous commits are only formed
where the loop has no safepoint, which with poll insertion on means nowhere:
every loop gets a poll on its back edge. A loop that cannot allocate or call
and provably terminates does not need that poll for liveness -- the time to
the next poll is bounded by its trip count -- so -cmm-counted-loops removes it
and polls once on the loop's exits instead. Inside such a loop the pointer
passes run as they would on a unit compiled without polling.

Termination is proved, not assumed. A loop is counted when one integer
parameter is stepped by the same constant n <> 0 on every back edge, and one
test `x R B` dominates all back edges, with x = m * counter + k and B
loop-invariant. With d = m * n the loop terminates if

  x < B,  d > 0:  B <= max_int - d + 1     x > B,  d < 0:  B >= min_int - d - 1
  x <= B, d > 0:  B <= max_int - d         x >= B, d < 0:  B >= min_int - d
  x <> B, |d| = 2^k:  x0 <= B and (B - x0) land (|d| - 1) = 0
                      (x0 = x on entry; mirrored for d < 0)
  x = B:  always

since the counter cannot wrap past B. A condition that folds to true needs no
code; otherwise it is checked at loop entry and a renamed copy of the original
loop, polls kept, runs when it fails. In a nest, an inner check that does not
read the counter's entry value is lifted to the outer loop's entry, so the
whole nest runs poll-free behind one check.

A counted loop inside a loop that keeps its poll needs no exit poll, since
Cfg_polling polls that loop's back edge. A loop containing a polled loop is not
counted: a derived pointer would be live across that poll.

Also:
- A noalloc external call is not a safepoint: builtins are selected as
  instructions and other noalloc calls cannot reach the GC.
- Pointers into rows of vectors: a 128-bit unboxed-array access untags its
  index inside the address, (+a a (<< (>>s idx 1) 3)), which hid the counter
  from the pointer passes. Since (y + 2q) >>s 1 = (y >>s 1) + q whenever
  y + 2q does not overflow, which an index that addresses memory has not,
  accesses to one array share one carried pointer plus constant offsets.
- Cmm.static_handler gains is_bounded; Cfg_selectgen records bounded headers
  and Cfg_polling leaves their back edges alone.

-dcounted-loops prints each loop's decision.
